# Copy this file to .env and adjust as needed:
#   cp env.sample .env
#
# .env (repo root) is sourced automatically by scripts/lib/common.sh on
# every script invocation, via `set -a` -- so plain KEY=value lines (no
# `export` needed) are exported automatically. Precedence, lowest to
# highest:
#
#   1. System-level environment variables (e.g. /etc/profile.d/sandbox.sh,
#      see SETUP.md) -- the host-wide baseline.
#   2. .env in this repo -- overrides #1 for anyone using this checkout.
#   3. Flags passed to a script (e.g. `--ram` on 00_init_vm.sh) -- overrides
#      both, for a single invocation.
#
# .env is gitignored -- safe to keep host- or checkout-specific overrides
# here without risk of committing them.
#
# Only uncomment/set the variables you actually want to override; anything
# left commented out here falls through to the system-level value (or fails
# scripts/lib/common.sh's require_env check if nothing set it at all).

# SANDBOX_HOME="${SANDBOX_HOME:-$HOME/projects}"
# LIBVIRT_HOME="${STORAGE_POOL_HOME:-$SANDBOX_HOME/libvirt}"
# STORAGE_POOL_IMAGES="${LIBVIRT_HOME}/images"
# STORAGE_POOL_ISOS="${LIBVIRT_HOME}/isos"
# STORAGE_POOL_DISKS="${LIBVIRT_HOME}/disks"
# STORAGE_POOL_SNAPSHOTS="${LIBVIRT_HOME}/snapshots"
# STORAGE_POOL_CLOUD_INIT_ISOS="${LIBVIRT_HOME}/cloud-init"

# DEFAULT_CLOUD_IMG="noble-server-cloudimg-amd64"
# DEFAULT_OS_VARIANT="ubuntu24.04"
# DEFAULT_RAM_MB="2048"
# DEFAULT_VCPUS="2"
# DEFAULT_DISK_GB="20"

# DEFAULT_AUTOSTART="false"

# Used for SSH connection hints (vmname.<tailnet>.ts.net) and the
# ssh-keygen -R reminder printed by 04_destroy_vm.sh. Set this to your tailnet
# name, e.g. "tailnet-name.ts.net" or leave unset if you don't use Tailscale.
# TAILSCALE_TAILNET=""

# Consumed by scripts/11_configure_vm.sh to join a VM to your
# tailnet (also gates enabling UFW -- see that script's header comment).
# Generate a reusable/ephemeral, tagged key at
# https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys -- treat it as a secret,
# never commit it. Can also be passed per-invocation via --authkey instead.
# TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY=""

# Consumed by scripts/04_destroy_vm.sh (via scripts/lib/tailscale_api.sh) to
# deregister a VM's device from the tailnet on teardown, so a
# destroy-then-recreate cycle with the same VM name reliably reclaims the
# same hostname instead of colliding with a stale device record left behind
# until Tailscale's own ephemeral cleanup gets to it. Optional -- if unset,
# 04_destroy_vm.sh just skips this step (logged, not fatal).
#
# Create an OAuth client at https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/oauth
# scoped to "Devices Core" -> Write only, and restrict it to the tag(s) your
# sandbox VMs use (e.g. tag:dmz-ephemeral) -- that way this credential can
# only ever delete devices carrying that tag, nothing else on the tailnet.
# Treat both as secrets, never commit them.
# TAILSCALE_API_CLIENT_ID=""
# TAILSCALE_API_CLIENT_SECRET=""
